---
// THE POLICY SECTION. Facts from merchant config, words derived from facts.
//
// ─── WHAT IT USED TO READ ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// `product.guarantee` — days, title, text and a three-point list, all copy.
// It rendered "Garantía de 30 días", "te devolvemos el dinero. Sin vueltas.",
// and promised a "Devolución simple", a "Reembolso completo" and one "sin
// preguntas". Nothing configured the 30 and nothing supported a single one of
// those conditions; they are exactly the adjectives lib/policy.ts refuses to
// derive, because no field states them.
//
// ─── THE DISTINCTION THIS SECTION NOW KEEPS ───────────────────────────────
//
// A RETURNS WINDOW is what the merchant configured. A COMMERCIAL GUARANTEE is
// an ADDITIONAL promise, optional, and absent unless configured — absent means
// absent, never 30. Collapsing the two is how a page ends up claiming a
// guarantee it never made. So the headline states returns, and the guarantee
// line appears only when there is one.
//
// ─── PREVIEW RENDERS NOTHING ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// With no merchant there are no policy facts, and a policy section with no
// facts is decoration that invites a default. The section is omitted whole
// rather than shown empty. This is a structural change the fingerprint must
// see, and it is the correct one: a preview landing genuinely has no policy
// to state.
//
// ─── THE SHELL IS PRESERVED ───────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Same id, same surface, same rhythm, same seal, same centred container, same
// three-column grid of icon-over-text cells. Only the sentences changed, and
// the cells are now built from facts instead of a copy array.
//
// ─── ALWAYS THREE CELLS, NEVER A FOURTH FACT INVENTED TO GET THERE ────────
//
// This used to be `[returnShippingLine, shippingLine, ...(guaranteeLine ? [x] : [])]`
// — two cells for most merchants, since a commercial guarantee is optional and
// most have not configured one. A `sm:grid-cols-3` grid with two children is
// not a design choice, it is a hole. The third slot is the delivery ETA when
// there is no additional guarantee to state, and the guarantee headline when
// there is one — both are real, configured facts, so the slot is always
// filled and never by something nobody configured.
//
// ─── THE ICON STAYS THE SEALED SHIELD — DISTINCT ICONS ARE OUT OF SCOPE HERE
//
// This was going to give each cell an icon matching its own meaning: `check`
// for the returns promise, `truck` for who ships it, `shield` kept for the
// guarantee. It does not, and the reason is load-bearing rather than
// cosmetic: ASTRAVIBE_FIXED_STRUCTURAL_GRAMMAR_V1 declares exactly ONE shape
// for this repeatable region (id `guarantee/cells`), and that declared shape
// is the shield SVG's own `d` path, verbatim, as part of what "this region"
// structurally IS. `contract.fixed-grammar-seal.test.ts`'s "every declared
// region normalized" caught it immediately: a second icon shape makes the
// region render as raw, unrecognised markup instead of collapsing into the
// sealed token, which is precisely the defect a seal exists to surface.
//
// Varying icon SHAPE per cell is therefore a GRAMMAR change, not a template
// one — a new version (V4) would need to declare `guarantee/cells` as a set
// of named shapes the way V3 already does for `comparison/rows`, get its own
// artifact and its own reviewed seal, and that is a deliberate step for
// whoever owns the grammar to take on purpose, not something to fold into an
// unrelated presentation fix. What this fix DOES keep: three real cells,
// always — see below — with the one icon the seal actually recognises.
import Container from '@/components/ui/Container.astro';
import { ICONS } from '@/lib/icons';
import {
  policy,
  returnsHeadline,
  returnShippingLine,
  commercialGuaranteeHeadline,
  shippingLine,
  carrierLine,
} from '@/lib/policy';

const facts = policy;

// Derived once so the section cannot disagree with itself.
const headline = facts ? returnsHeadline(facts) : null;
const guaranteeLine = facts ? commercialGuaranteeHeadline(facts) : null;

const cells = facts
  ? [returnShippingLine(facts), carrierLine(facts), guaranteeLine ?? shippingLine(facts)]
  : [];
---

{
  facts && headline && (
    <section id="garantia" class="scroll-mt-4 bg-gold-tint py-12 md:py-16">
      <Container class="text-center">
        {/*
          THE SEAL, WITH A FALLBACK THAT CANNOT 404. `onerror` swaps a broken
          image for the same shield glyph already used elsewhere on this page
          — inline markup, not a second network request, so there is nothing
          left for the fallback ITSELF to fail to load. alt describes the
          seal, not a day count it would otherwise have to invent when no
          commercial guarantee is configured.
        */}
        <span class="relative mx-auto flex size-28 items-center justify-center">
          <img
            src="/sello-garantia.webp"
            width="112"
            height="112"
            alt="Sello de garantía"
            class="size-28"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            onerror="this.style.display='none';this.nextElementSibling.style.display='flex'"
          />
          <span class="hidden size-28 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-gold/15" style="display:none">
            <svg viewBox={ICONS.shield.viewBox} class="size-16 text-gold" aria-hidden="true">
              <path fill="currentColor" d={ICONS.shield.path} />
            </svg>
          </span>
        </span>

        <h2 class="mt-4 text-display md:text-4xl">{headline}</h2>
        <p class="mx-auto mt-2 max-w-md text-sm text-steel">{returnShippingLine(facts)}</p>

        <div class="mx-auto mt-8 grid max-w-lg grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
          {cells.map((cell) => (
            <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-2 text-xs text-graphite">
              <svg viewBox={ICONS.shield.viewBox} class="size-6 text-gold" aria-hidden="true">
                <path fill="currentColor" d={ICONS.shield.path} />
              </svg>
              <span>{cell}</span>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </Container>
    </section>
  )
}
